/*  Notes the checker writes onto the tree — what C#'s checker sets on a node outside its
    constructor: an axiom's language, the type an `is a` test was asked of, the function a sort
    keys on. The checked tree prints them as `:Name value`, after the fields.

    ★ IN PLACE, as C# writes them: a node's children are its own series, so a note written here
    is in the program `--tree` prints, with nothing to thread back up.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The notes a kind of node can carry, in the order its C# record declares them — the order
    /// `ParserTreePrinter` prints them in.
    Bind series of text to note-order, given (the text kind):
        Judge kind, where it is:
            "AxiomLiteral", return a series of text with (":Language", ":Parameters", ":ReturnType", ":ReleasedBy", ":ReleaseAxiom").
            "CastExpression", return a series of text with (":NamedArgs", ":ResolvedFunctionName", ":RunsAxiom", ":RunsAxiomValue").
            "CastStatement",
                return a series of text with (":NamedArgs", ":ResolvedFunctionName", ":RunsAxiom", ":RunsAxiomValue", ":PassesFailureOff").
            "ObjectLiteral", return a series of text with (":ResolvedTypeName", ":FilledDefaults").
            "IsTypeCheck", return a series of text with (":StaticTargetType").
            "SortExpression", return a series of text with (":KeyFunction").
            "ReturnStatement", return a series of text with (":RunsAxiom").
            Otherwise, return a series of text.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Replaces a node's `place`th field where it stands — C# setting a property its constructor took.
    Bind void to rewrite-field, given (the node target, the number place, the node value):
        The item place of target's children becomes value.
    Done.

    /// Writes `mark` onto `target` as `value`, replacing any earlier note of that name — or, given
    /// nothing or a type not known (C#'s null), takes it off. C# rewrites these on every pass rather
    /// than adding to them, so writing one twice leaves one.
    Bind void to note, given (the node target, the text mark, the node value):
        Define fields as a series of node.
        Define held as a map from text to node.
        Define held-order as a series of text.
        Define index as 1.
        Define count as the number of target's children.
        While index is not greater than count, repeat:
            Define here as item index of target's children.
            If here's kind is "atom" and here's word starts with ":" and index is less than count:
                In held, the entry for here's word becomes item (index + 1) of target's children.
                Insert here's word into held-order.
                Increment index by 2.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Insert here into fields.
                Increment index by 1.
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast is-nothing on (value) or cast is-none on (value):
            If (the entry for mark in held) is not void, remove mark from held.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            If (the entry for mark in held) is void, insert mark into held-order.
            In held, the entry for mark becomes value.
        Done.
        // ⚠ A mark the order does not list is kept, after the rest — never dropped.
        Define ordered as cast note-order on (target's kind).
        Define listed-names as a map from text to fact.
        For each name in ordered, repeat:
            In listed-names, the entry for name becomes true.
        Done.
        For each name in held-order, repeat:
            If (the entry for name in listed-names) is void, insert name into ordered.
        Done.
        While the number of target's children is greater than 0, repeat:
            Remove item 1 from target's children.
        Done.
        For each field in fields, repeat:
            Insert field into target's children.
        Done.
        For each name in ordered, repeat:
            Define value-held as the entry for name in held.
            If value-held is not void:
                Insert cast atom on (name) into target's children.
                Insert value-held into target's children.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
